I"�<h3 id="how-to-remove-a-network-oracle-rac-19c">How to remove a network oracle rac 19c</h3>
<p>In this tutorial we’re going to remove network 2 configuration from an Oracle RAC cluster.</p>

<h4 id="get-network-info-that-you-want-to-remove">Get network info that you want to remove</h4>
<div class="highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code>srvctl config network -netnum 2
srvctl config scan -netnum 2
srvctl config scan_listener -all
srvctl config listener -listener LISTENER_SRV
srvctl config vip -node db-01
</code></pre></div></div>

<h4 id="stop-all-network-services-that-were-going-to-remove">Stop all network services that we’re going to remove</h4>
<div class="highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code>srvctl stop scan -force -netnum 2 
srvctl stop listener -listener LISTENER_SRV
srvctl stop scan_listener -netnum 2
srvctl stop vip -vip db-01-vip.srv
srvctl stop vip -vip db-02-vip.srv
</code></pre></div></div>
<h4 id="remove-the-services">Remove the services</h4>
<div class="highlighter-rouge"><div class="highlight"><pre class="highlight"><code>srvctl remove scan_listener -netnum 2
srvctl remove scan -netnum 2
srvctl remove listener -listener LISTENER_SRV
sudo /app/grid/19.3.0/bin/srvctl remove scan -netnum 2 -force
sudo /app/grid/19.3.0/bin/srvctl remove network -netnum 2 -force
sudo /app/grid/19.3.0/bin/srvctl remove vip -vip db-01-vip.srv
sudo /app/grid/19.3.0/bin/srvctl remove vip -vip db-02-vip.srv
</code></pre></div></div>
